+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Native MCP clients send the standard `_meta` field (for example `{"progressToken": ...}`) in
+`tools/call` params. The task-handoff stdio adapter
+(`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py --mcp-stdio`) allows only `name` and `arguments` in
+`params`, so every `tools/call` from such clients is rejected with `invalid request` before
+dispatch, and no tool call over stdio works for them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `tools/call` accepts a top-level `_meta` field when its value is a JSON object; the value is
+  ignored at dispatch (the adapter reads only `name` and `arguments`).
+- Every other unknown top-level `params` field still fails closed with JSON-RPC
+  `-32602 invalid request`; a `_meta` whose value is not an object is rejected the same way.
+- The identity-override refusal (tool arguments cannot replace the host/session binding) and the
+  oversized/unterminated-frame refusal (sanitized `-32600`, transport closes, remaining bytes
+  never become another request) keep working exactly as they do today.
+- The Codex companion copy `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py` receives the same
+  bytes and stays byte-identical to `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py`.
+- `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py` gains coverage that a `_meta` call dispatches,
+  that a different unknown `params` field still fails, and that the companion copy stays
+  byte-identical.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `task-handoff-mcp`: the stdio MCP transport of the explicit task-handoff adapter — the accepted
+  `tools/call` param shape, the fail-closed unknown-field policy, the environment-only identity
+  binding, bounded frames, and the byte-identical companion-copy shipping contract.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+(none — this is the project's first capability spec)
+
+## Impact
+
+- Code: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py` (the `tools/call` branch of `_mcp_stdio`),
+  `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py` (byte-identical companion),
+  `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py` (new stdio test cases).
+- Protocol surface: the `tools/call` params allow-list gains `_meta` (object values only).
+  `initialize`, `ping`, `tools/list`, the per-tool argument validation, the advertised
+  `protocolVersion` (2025-06-18), and all JSON-RPC error codes are unchanged.
+- Docs: one-sentence clarification in `plugins/graphhelm/README.md` where it states that "unknown
+  fields fail closed" (that statement stays true; the `_meta` exception becomes explicit).
+- No plugin version bump in this change: the existing test pins `serverInfo.version` to
+  `plugin.json`'s `version`, and the request does not ask for a release.
+- No dependencies added or changed; runtime environment requirements are unchanged.
